The kits design passed on its fifth attempt and its worker is running. It took about 25 minutes of revisions. The lesson I logged: features that add new mechanics need a tighter design section before launch. All three runs are active now:
- `sea-compact-fixes`: worker running;
- `encounters-core`: waiting on its candidate check and review;
- `fruit-kits-core`: worker running.

The `docking-feel` worker finished in about 21 minutes and applied the operator addendum, so the hull-footprint rule is in. It also:
- removed the land spur (all four mirrored copies go with it, and every map validator still passes);
- moved the map-sketch writer into the typechecked build script;
- added the head-on, pinch-guard and behind-land tests.

Verification is running now.

The economy hardening is merged (`0fd0f2f`), and typecheck plus all 844 unit tests pass.

`main` now has:
- the compact sea;
- the encounter rules;
- the Ember and Smoke kits;
- the ruins;
- the full, hardened economy.

Still running: `encounters-online` (duels at sea) and `intel-core-fixes-2`.

`final-island` is approved by both reviewers and integrated (`832b0fd`). Merging it into `main` and running the non-browser checks now. I'll run the browser suite later, once `encounters-online` isn't using the ports.

**The final islands are on `main`.** Its browser run is in progress.

`main` now has:
